<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Cheyenne.jpg" alt="Portrait of Cheyenne" width="450" height="354" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Cheyenne. 11x14, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Before staring this sketch portrait I made a note for myself to use delicate paint handling and keep the key at a high value. The portrait that I did earlier in the year, before she passed, of our dog Hannah was a great help in establishing the palette and overall approach that I used for Cheyenne.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">After doing the block-in the day before, I completed the portrait in its entirety the next day in one long painting session.</p>
